# Answer key for B6 t4_adversarial.sql - set-returning and table functions, adversarial.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, plus D-26..D-28. Every node is schema-qualified.
# S3's element and S5's whole statement have no source and no boundary - checked in the
# report, not expressible here.

@ 19 S1 element named like a source column
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.kpi_rollup.level derived
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
forbid value staging.orders.channel -> mart.kpi_rollup.level identity | t.channel is the tag, not the orders column

@ 27 S2 SRF alias named like a real table
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.top_customers.region derived
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
forbid filter staging.orders.customer_id -> mart.top_customers | the ON is structural (D-5)

@ 37 S3 a literal array
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.channel_mix.region identity

@ 45 S4 an SRF over a scalar subquery
value staging.products.brand, staging.products.status -> mart.product_performance.category_name aggregated
note array_agg is on the path; the subquery's WHERE is a value of what it feeds (D-12).

@ 56 S5 a series of literals only

@ 63 S6 an unnest that multiplies a COUNT (D-27)
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value staging.orders.id -> mart.channel_mix.orders aggregated
influence staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.orders
forbid influence staging.orders.tags -> mart.channel_mix.orders | the unnest repeats rows but names no column (D-27)

@ 72 S7 TABLESAMPLE ... REPEATABLE
value staging.payments.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue identity
filter staging.payments.method -> mart.channel_mix

@ 81 S8 a CTE named unnest beside the function
value staging.customers.segment -> mart.customer_summary.segment identity
value staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary.status derived

@ 94 S9 an element named like its array
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.customer_summary.region derived
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.customer_summary.full_name derived

@ 102 S10 an SRF inside an IN subquery
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
filter staging.orders.tags -> mart.channel_mix
note 'vip' IN (SELECT unnest(o.tags)) decides which orders land: a filter from the array.

@ 111 S11 a series between two timestamp columns
value staging.shipments.shipped_at, staging.shipments.delivered_at -> mart.sales_daily.sale_date derived
value staging.shipments.warehouse_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
